# Wireframes — WebSocket UI Components

## Purpose & Flow Context

These wireframes define the structural layout for WebSocket-related UI components in the Linear App Clone. They serve the WebSocket Authentication, Channel Subscription, Event Processing, Error Handling, and Connection Status Display flows.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Screen Inventory

| Flow | Screen | States Visited | Wireframe Section |
|------|--------|----------------|-------------------|
| WebSocket: Authentication | App Layout | loading, connected, disconnected, error | §1 |
| WebSocket: Authentication | Connection Error Modal | hidden, visible | §2 |
| WebSocket: Channel Subscription | App Layout | subscribed, unsubscribed | §1 |
| WebSocket: Event Processing | App Layout | idle, updating | §1 |
| WebSocket: Event Processing | Issue Board | idle, issue-updated | §5 |
| WebSocket: Event Processing | Notification Panel | idle, new-notification | §6 |
| WebSocket: Event Processing | Comment Thread | idle, new-comment | §7 |
| WebSocket: Error Handling | Connection Error Modal | hidden, visible | §2 |
| WebSocket: Error Handling | Error Toast | hidden, visible | §3 |
| WebSocket: Connection Status Display | Header | connected, connecting, reconnecting, disconnected | §4 |

---

## §1 App Layout — WebSocket Integration

### Purpose & Flow Context

Main application shell that hosts the WebSocket connection status indicator and manages real-time event processing. Serves as the entry point for all WebSocket flows.

### Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm intent.

**App-shell**: Shared header + nav + container. Regions:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Logo, Navigation, ConnectionStatusIndicator, UserMenu | Sticky top, full width |
| Main Content | Primary application content | 12-column grid, max-width 1200px |
| Toast Container | Error/Revert/Reconnection toasts | Fixed bottom-right, z-index 40 |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Connection Status Indicator (header)
2. Primary application content
3. Toast notifications (bottom-right)

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]    [Nav Items]    [ConnectionStatusIndicator]  [User]  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  +-----------------------------+  +-----------------------------+  |
|  |  {Main Content Area}       |  |  {Sidebar (if applicable)} |  |
|  |                             |  |                             |  |
|  |  [Primary Content]          |  |  [Secondary Content]        |  |
|  |                             |  |                             |  |
|  +-----------------------------+  +-----------------------------+  |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                          +-- Toast Container ----+|
|                                          | [Error Toast]         ||
|                                          | [Revert Toast]        ||
|                                          | [Reconnection Toast]  ||
|                                          +-----------------------+|
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| ConnectionStatusIndicator | ConnectionStatusIndicator | Displays colored dot based on WebSocket state | Compact variant in header |
| Toast Container | ToastContainer | Renders active toasts in stack | Max 3 visible, oldest dismissed |
| Error Toast | WebSocketErrorToast | Auto-dismiss after 5s | Rate limited shows countdown |
| Revert Toast | RevertToast | Auto-dismiss after 10s | Undo button reverts change |
| Reconnection Toast | ReconnectionToast | Shows during reconnect, auto-dismiss on success | Transparent background, informational only |

### Data Display

This screen hosts dynamic content that updates via WebSocket events. The main content area displays issue boards, comment threads, and notification panels that receive real-time updates.

### Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Connection Status | "Connected" / "Connecting" / "Reconnecting" / "Disconnected" | Screen reader accessible |
| Error Toast Title | "Rate limited" / "Invalid channel" | Clear, actionable language |
| Revert Toast Message | "Change reverted" | Explains what happened |

### States

#### Populated (Default)

The application is connected and receiving real-time updates. ConnectionStatusIndicator shows green dot. Content updates seamlessly.

#### Loading

Application is establishing WebSocket connection. ConnectionStatusIndicator shows yellow pulsing dot.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]    [Nav Items]    [● pulsing]              [User]      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  +-----------------------------+  +-----------------------------+  |
|  |  [===== skeleton bar =====] |  |  [==== skeleton ===]       |  |
|  |  [==== skeleton bar =====]  |  |                             |  |
|  +-----------------------------+  +-----------------------------+  |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### Error

WebSocket connection fails. ConnectionErrorModal appears for critical errors. Error toast for transient errors.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]    [Nav Items]    [● red]                    [User]    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  +-----------------------------+  +-----------------------------+  |
|  |  [Connection Error Modal]   |  |  {Sidebar (dimmed)}        |  |
|  |                             |  |                             |  |
|  |  Authentication failed      |  |                             |  |
|  |  [Return to Login]          |  |                             |  |
|  +-----------------------------+  +-----------------------------+  |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### Success / Confirmation

Connection established successfully. ConnectionStatusIndicator transitions from yellow to green. Brief "Connected" toast may appear.

### Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full layout as described |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Sidebar collapses to icons, toast container moves to top-right |
| Mobile (<768px) | Nav → hamburger, ConnectionStatusIndicator moves to status bar |

### Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | header, main, complementary (sidebar), contentinfo |
| Heading order | h1 for page title, h2 for sections |
| Reading / Focus order | Header → Main → Sidebar → Toast Container |
| Accessible names | ConnectionStatusIndicator has aria-label with status text |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through header items, main content, sidebar |
| Target size | All interactive elements ≥24×24 CSS px |
| Focus not obscured | Toast container positioned to not obscure focused elements |
| Non-color intent | ConnectionStatusIndicator uses icon + text, not color alone |

---

## §2 Connection Error Modal

### Purpose & Flow Context

Modal dialog displayed for critical WebSocket errors (auth_failed, invalid_token, forbidden, session.revoked). Blocks interaction until dismissed. Entry: WebSocket error received. Exit: Return to Login button clicked.

### Layout Regions

**Grid**: Modal overlay on 12-column grid. Modal content max-width 400px, centered.

**Modal Structure**:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Overlay | Backdrop blur, click to dismiss (if allowed) | Fixed position, z-index 50 |
| Modal Content | Header, Body, Footer | Centered, rounded corners |
| Modal Header | Icon + Title | Flex row |
| Modal Body | Error message | Plain language explanation |
| Modal Footer | Action buttons | Primary action (Return to Login) |

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  {Modal Overlay - backdrop blur}         |
|                                          |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |  [Icon]  {Error Title}             |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |                                    |  |
|  |  {Error message in plain language} |  |
|  |                                    |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |  [Return to Login]                 |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|                                          |
+------------------------------------------+
```

### Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Modal Overlay | ConnectionErrorModal | Click outside to dismiss (if not critical) | Critical errors require button click |
| Modal Header | ConnectionErrorModal | Icon + title based on error type | Icon color indicates severity |
| Modal Body | ConnectionErrorModal | Plain language error message | No raw error codes |
| Modal Footer | ConnectionErrorModal | Single action button | Focus trapped within modal |

### Data Display

This modal displays error information only. No dynamic data updates while modal is visible.

### Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Modal Title | "Authentication failed" / "Invalid token" / "Access denied" / "Session expired" | Clear, user-friendly |
| Modal Body | Explains what happened and what to do next | No technical jargon |
| Button Label | "Return to Login" | Clear call to action |

### States

#### Hidden

Modal is not rendered. Application functions normally.

#### Visible — auth_failed

Authentication failed. Tokens cleared. User must return to login.

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  {Modal Overlay - backdrop blur}         |
|                                          |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |  [⚠️]  Authentication failed       |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |                                    |  |
|  |  Your session has expired or the  |  |
|  |  token is invalid. Please log in  |  |
|  |  again.                           |  |
|  |                                    |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |  [Return to Login]                 |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|                                          |
+------------------------------------------+
```

#### Visible — forbidden

Access denied. No reconnect attempted. User must return to login.

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  {Modal Overlay - backdrop blur}         |
|                                          |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |  [🚫]  Access denied               |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |                                    |  |
|  |  You don't have permission to     |  |
|  |  access this resource.            |  |
|  |                                    |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |  [Return to Login]                 |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|                                          |
+------------------------------------------+
```

#### Visible — session.revoked

Session revoked by server. Tokens cleared. User must return to login.

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  {Modal Overlay - backdrop blur}         |
|                                          |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |  [⏰]  Session expired             |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |                                    |  |
|  |  Your session has been revoked.   |  |
|  |  Please log in again.             |  |
|  |                                    |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|  |  [Return to Login]                 |  |
|  +------------------------------------+  |
|                                          |
+------------------------------------------+
```

### Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Modal centered, max-width 400px |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Modal centered, full-width on small tablets |
| Mobile (<768px) | Modal full-width, padded for touch targets |

### Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | dialog role replaces landmarks within modal |
| Heading order | Modal title is h2 (page h1 is behind overlay) |
| Reading / Focus order | Focus trapped within modal, Tab cycles through focusable elements |
| Accessible names | Modal has aria-labelledby pointing to title |
| Keyboard operability | Escape closes modal (if allowed), Tab cycles focus |
| Target size | Button ≥44×44 CSS px (SC 2.5.8) |
| Focus not obscured | Modal content fully visible, focus ring visible |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, not color alone |

---

## §3 WebSocket Error Toast

### Purpose & Flow Context

Toast notification for transient WebSocket errors (rate_limited, invalid_channel). Auto-dismisses after timeout. Entry: Error received from server. Exit: Auto-dismiss or manual dismiss.

### Layout Regions

**Grid**: Toast container fixed bottom-right, z-index 40.

**Toast Structure**:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Toast Container | Stack of active toasts | Fixed position, flex column, gap 8px |
| Toast Content | Icon + Message + Dismiss button | Flex row |
| Toast Progress | Auto-dismiss countdown bar | Progress indicator |

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  [Icon]  {Error message}        [X]    |
|  [====================================] |
+------------------------------------------+
```

### Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Toast Icon | WebSocketErrorToast | Indicates error type | Color + icon for non-color intent |
| Toast Message | WebSocketErrorToast | Plain language error | Truncates at max-width |
| Dismiss Button | WebSocketErrorToast | Manual dismiss | Focus ring visible |
| Progress Bar | WebSocketErrorToast | Auto-dismiss countdown | Visual indicator of time remaining |

### Data Display

This toast displays error information only. No dynamic data updates while toast is visible.

### Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Toast Title | "Rate limited" / "Invalid channel" | Clear, concise |
| Toast Message | "Retry after X seconds" / "Subscription failed" | Actionable information |
| Dismiss Button | "Dismiss" (aria-label) | Accessible label |

### States

#### Hidden

Toast is not rendered. No errors to display.

#### Visible — rate_limited

Rate limit exceeded. Shows countdown for retry.

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  [⏰]  Rate limited              [X]    |
|         Retry after 30 seconds          |
|  [========================              ] |
+------------------------------------------+
```

#### Visible — invalid_channel

Invalid channel subscription. Auto-dismisses after 5s.

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  [🚫]  Invalid channel           [X]    |
|         Subscription failed             |
|  [====================================] |
+------------------------------------------+
```

### Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Toast bottom-right, max-width 360px |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Toast bottom-right, full-width on small tablets |
| Mobile (<768px) | Toast top, full-width, padded for touch |

### Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | toast role, no landmark required |
| Heading order | N/A (toast content) |
| Reading / Focus order | Focus moves to toast when it appears |
| Accessible names | Dismiss button has aria-label |
| Keyboard operability | Escape dismisses toast, Tab to dismiss button |
| Target size | Dismiss button ≥24×24 CSS px |
| Focus not obscured | Toast positioned to not obscure focused elements |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, not color alone |

---

## §4 Header — Connection Status Indicator

### Purpose & Flow Context

Application header displaying WebSocket connection status as a colored indicator. Serves the Connection Status Display flow. Entry: User views header. Exit: User navigates away.

### Layout Regions

**Grid**: Header spans full width, 12-column grid internally.

**Header Structure**:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Logo | Application logo | Left-aligned |
| Navigation | Primary nav items | Center-aligned |
| ConnectionStatusIndicator | Colored dot + status | Right-aligned, before user menu |
| UserMenu | User avatar + dropdown | Right-aligned |

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]    [Nav Items]    [● status]              [Avatar ▼]   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| ConnectionStatusIndicator | ConnectionStatusIndicator | Compact variant, 8px dot | Pulsing animation when connecting |
| Status Text | Screen reader only | aria-label with status text | Visually hidden |

### Data Display

The indicator displays the current WebSocket connection state. No dynamic data updates while header is static.

### Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Status Text | "Connected" / "Connecting" / "Reconnecting" / "Disconnected" | Screen reader accessible |

### States

#### Connected

WebSocket connected. Green static dot.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]    [Nav Items]    [● green]                [Avatar ▼]   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### Connecting

WebSocket establishing connection. Yellow pulsing dot.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]    [Nav Items]    [● yellow pulsing]        [Avatar ▼]   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### Reconnecting

WebSocket reconnecting after disconnect. Yellow pulsing dot.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]    [Nav Items]    [● yellow pulsing]        [Avatar ▼]   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

> **Note**: Connecting and Reconnecting share the same yellow pulsing dot — intentional per spec. Semantic difference carried by `aria-label` per the accessibility table below.

#### Disconnected

WebSocket disconnected. Red static dot.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]    [Nav Items]    [● red]                   [Avatar ▼]   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full header layout as described |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Navigation collapses to icons, indicator remains visible |
| Mobile (<768px) | Navigation → hamburger, indicator moves to status bar |

### Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | header landmark |
| Heading order | N/A (header region) |
| Reading / Focus order | Logo → Navigation → Indicator → UserMenu |
| Accessible names | ConnectionStatusIndicator has aria-label with status text |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through header items |
| Target size | All interactive elements ≥24×24 CSS px |
| Focus not Obscured | Header sticky, indicator always visible |
| Non-color intent | Indicator uses icon + text, not color alone |

---

## §5 Issue Board — Real-Time Updates

### Purpose & Flow Context

Board view displaying issues in columns (by status). Receives real-time updates via WebSocket when issues are created, updated, or deleted. Entry: User navigates to Issue Board. Exit: User clicks an issue to open detail.

### Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout within the App Layout shell. Board uses horizontal scroll for columns.

**Board Structure**:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Board Header | Title, filters, view toggle | 12-column, full width |
| Board Columns | Status-grouped columns (Todo, In Progress, Done) | Horizontal flex, scroll overflow |
| Issue Card | Issue title, assignee, priority, labels | Card within column |
| Toast Container | RevertToast on failed optimistic update | Fixed bottom-right (from §1) |

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  {Issue Board Header}                                             |
|  [Filters ▼]  [View: Board]                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +-- Todo ----------+  +-- In Progress ---+  +-- Done ----------+ |
|  |                  |  |                  |  |                  | |
|  |  [Issue Card]    |  |  [Issue Card]    |  |  [Issue Card]    | |
|  |  [Issue Card]    |  |  [Issue Card]    |  |                  | |
|  |                  |  |                  |  |                  | |
|  +------------------+  +------------------+  +------------------+ |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Issue Card | Generic card ⚠ | Click opens issue detail | Hover shows quick actions; hover triggers optimistic update on drag |
| Board Column | Generic container ⚠ | Scrollable vertically | Empty column shows placeholder |
| Board Header | Generic header ⚠ | Filter and view controls | Sticky on scroll |

> ⚠ **DS gap**: No card component exists in the design-system. The Issue Card is a generic layout element. The design-system owner should define a `Card` component before the hi-fi pass. See Assumption 8.
>
> ⚠ **DS gap (optional)**: "Generic container" (Board Column) is a flex column with `overflow-y: auto`, `gap: 8px`. "Generic header" (Board Header) is a flex row with filter/view controls, `position: sticky`, `top: 0`. These are structural layout elements not defined in the DS. The DS owner may optionally define `Container` and `Header` components for consistency. See Assumption 9.

### Data Display

**Data density**: Medium — cards with key metadata (title, assignee, priority, labels).

**Card layout**: Vertical list within columns, sortable by drag-and-drop.

**Progressive disclosure**: Card shows title + assignee + priority + labels; full details on click.

### Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Board Title | "Issues" | Page heading |
| Column Headers | "Todo" / "In Progress" / "Done" | Status group names |
| Empty Column | "No issues" | When column has zero items |

### States

#### Idle (Default)

Board populated with issues. Columns show cards in their respective status groups.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  {Issue Board Header}                                             |
|  [Filters ▼]  [View: Board]                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +-- Todo ----------+  +-- In Progress ---+  +-- Done ----------+ |
|  |                  |  |                  |  |                  | |
|  |  [Issue Card]    |  |  [Issue Card]    |  |  [Issue Card]    | |
|  |  [Issue Card]    |  |                  |  |                  | |
|  |                  |  |                  |  |                  | |
|  +------------------+  +------------------+  +------------------+ |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### Issue Updated

An issue receives a real-time update (status change, title edit, assignee change). The card visually updates with a brief highlight animation to indicate the change. If the issue moves columns, it animates to the new position.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  {Issue Board Header}                                             |
|  [Filters ▼]  [View: Board]                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +-- Todo ----------+  +-- In Progress ---+  +-- Done ----------+ |
|  |                  |  |                  |  |                  | |
|  |  [Issue Card]    |  |  [Issue Card]    |  |  [Issue Card]    | |
|  |  [Issue Card] ~~~|→ |                  |  |                  | |
|  |                  |  |                  |  |                  | |
|  +------------------+  +------------------+  +------------------+ |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
                          ~~~ = card animates to new column
```

#### Empty

No issues exist. Shows empty state with call-to-action to create first issue.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  {Issue Board Header}                                             |
|  [Filters ▼]  [View: Board]                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  No issues yet. Create your first issue to get started.           |
|                                                                    |
|  [Create Issue]                                                   |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full board layout as described |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Columns collapse to 2 visible, horizontal scroll |
| Mobile (<768px) | Board → list view (single column, scrollable) |

### Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | main landmark, header within board |
| Heading order | h1 for "Issues", h2 for column headers |
| Reading / Focus order | Board header → Columns (left to right) → Cards (top to bottom) |
| Accessible names | Issue cards have aria-label with issue title |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through cards, Enter/Space opens detail, Arrow keys navigate columns |
| Target size | Issue cards ≥24×24 CSS px touch target |
| Focus not obscured | Board header sticky, cards scroll beneath |
| Non-color intent | Issue status shown via column position + label, not color alone |

---

## §6 Notification Panel — Real-Time Updates

### Purpose & Flow Context

Panel displaying user notifications (issue mentions, assignments, comments). Receives real-time updates via WebSocket when new notifications arrive. Entry: User clicks notification bell. Exit: User clicks notification to navigate to source.

### Layout Regions

**Grid**: Panel overlays 12-column grid, max-width 400px, right-aligned.

**Panel Structure**:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Panel Header | Title, mark-all-read, close | Flex row |
| Notification List | Scrollable list of notifications | Vertical flex |
| Notification Item | Icon, message, timestamp, source | Flex row |
| Empty State | No notifications message | Centered content |

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  Notifications         [Mark all] [X]   |
+------------------------------------------+
|  [Icon] {Notification message}   2m ago |
|  [Icon] {Notification message}   1h ago |
|  [Icon] {Notification message}   3h ago |
|  ...                                    |
+------------------------------------------+
```

### Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Notification Item | Generic list item ⚠ | Click navigates to source | Unread items have bold indicator |
| Panel Header | Generic header ⚠ | Close panel on X | — |
| Mark All Read | Button | Marks all as read | Disables when no unread |

> ⚠ **DS gap (optional)**: "Generic list item" (Notification Item) is a flex row with icon + message + timestamp, `padding: 8px`, unread indicator via bold text (not color alone). "Generic header" (Panel Header) is a flex row with title + close button. These are structural layout elements not defined in the DS. The DS owner may optionally define `ListItem` and `Header` components for consistency. See Assumption 9.

### Data Display

**Data density**: Medium — list items with icon, message, timestamp.

**List layout**: Vertical list, newest first, scrollable overflow.

**Progressive disclosure**: Notification shows icon + message + timestamp; full context on click.

### Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Panel Title | "Notifications" | Panel heading |
| Mark All Read | "Mark all read" | Button label |
| Empty State | "No notifications" | When list is empty |
| Timestamp | Relative time ("2m ago", "1h ago") | Human-readable |

### States

#### Idle (Populated)

Panel populated with notifications. Unread items have bold indicator.

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  Notifications         [Mark all] [X]   |
+------------------------------------------+
|  ● [Icon] {Notification message}  2m ago |
|  ● [Icon] {Notification message}  1h ago |
|    [Icon] {Notification message}  3h ago |
|  ...                                    |
+------------------------------------------+
  ● = unread indicator
```

#### New Notification

A new notification arrives via WebSocket. The item animates in at the top of the list with a brief highlight. If panel is closed, the notification bell shows a badge count.

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  Notifications         [Mark all] [X]   |
+------------------------------------------+
|  ● [Icon] {New notification}     just now |  ← new item, highlighted
|  ● [Icon] {Notification message}  2m ago |
|  ● [Icon] {Notification message}  1h ago |
|  ...                                    |
+------------------------------------------+
```

#### Empty

No notifications exist. Shows empty state.

```
+------------------------------------------+
|  Notifications         [Mark all] [X]   |
+------------------------------------------+
|                                          |
|  No notifications yet.                   |
|                                          |
+------------------------------------------+
```

### Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Panel overlays content, max-width 400px, right-aligned |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Panel full-width on small tablets |
| Mobile (<768px) | Panel full-screen overlay, close button top-right |

### Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | dialog role for panel overlay |
| Heading order | Panel title is h2 |
| Reading / Focus order | Panel header → Notification list (top to bottom) |
| Accessible names | Notification items have aria-label with full message text |
| Keyboard operability | Escape closes panel, Tab through notifications, Enter/Space opens source |
| Target size | Notification items ≥24×24 CSS px touch target |
| Focus not obscured | Panel fully visible, focus ring visible |
| Non-color intent | Unread indicator uses icon + bold, not color alone |

---

## §7 Comment Thread — Real-Time Updates

### Purpose & Flow Context

Thread displaying comments on an issue. Receives real-time updates via WebSocket when new comments are added. Entry: User opens issue detail. Exit: User navigates away or collapses thread.

### Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout within the App Layout shell. Comment thread uses single column.

**Thread Structure**:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Thread Header | Issue title, status, metadata | Full width |
| Comment List | Scrollable list of comments | Vertical flex |
| Comment Item | Author, avatar, timestamp, body | Card-like layout |
| Comment Input | Text input, submit button | Sticky bottom |

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  {Issue Title} — {Status}                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|  |  [Avatar] {Author Name}              {Timestamp}            | |
|  |  {Comment body text here...}                                | |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|                                                                    |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|  |  [Avatar] {Author Name}              {Timestamp}            | |
|  |  {Comment body text here...}                                | |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Comment input field...]                          [Post]        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Comment Item | Generic card ⚠ | Author + timestamp + body | Long body truncates with expand |
| Comment Input | Text input + button | Submit on Enter or click | Empty input disables submit |
| Thread Header | Generic header ⚠ | Shows issue context | Sticky on scroll |

> ⚠ **DS gap**: No card component exists in the design-system. The Comment Item is a generic layout element. The design-system owner should define a `Card` component before the hi-fi pass. See Assumption 8.
>
> ⚠ **DS gap (optional)**: "Generic header" (Thread Header) is a flex row with issue title + status, `position: sticky`, `top: 0`. This is a structural layout element not defined in the DS. The DS owner may optionally define a `Header` component for consistency. See Assumption 9.

### Data Display

**Data density**: Medium — cards with author, timestamp, body text.

**List layout**: Vertical list, chronological order, scrollable overflow.

**Progressive disclosure**: Comment body shows first 3 lines; expand on click for full text.

### Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Thread Title | Issue title + status | Context for comments |
| Comment Author | User display name | Author of comment |
| Comment Timestamp | Relative time ("2m ago", "1h ago") | Human-readable |
| Comment Input | "Write a comment..." | Placeholder, not label |
| Submit Button | "Post" | Action label |

### States

#### Idle (Populated)

Thread populated with comments. Input ready for new comment.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  {Issue Title} — {Status}                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|  |  [Avatar] {Author Name}              {Timestamp}            | |
|  |  {Comment body text here...}                                | |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|                                                                    |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|  |  [Avatar] {Author Name}              {Timestamp}            | |
|  |  {Comment body text here...}                                | |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Write a comment...]                                [Post]      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### New Comment

A new comment arrives via WebSocket. The item animates in at the bottom of the list (or inline if reply). Brief highlight to indicate the new addition.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  {Issue Title} — {Status}                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|  |  [Avatar] {Author Name}              {Timestamp}            | |
|  |  {Comment body text here...}                                | |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|                                                                    |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|  |  [Avatar] {Author Name}              {Timestamp}            | |
|  |  {Comment body text here...}                                | |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|                                                                    |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|  |  [Avatar] {Author Name}              just now               | |
|  |  {New comment body...}  ← new, highlighted                  | |
|  +--------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Write a comment...]                                [Post]      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### Empty

No comments exist. Shows empty state with prompt to add first comment.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  {Issue Title} — {Status}                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  No comments yet. Be the first to comment.                       |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Write a comment...]                                [Post]      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full thread layout as described |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Thread full-width, comment input sticky |
| Mobile (<768px) | Thread full-width, input moves to bottom sheet |

### Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | main landmark, header within thread |
| Heading order | h1 for issue title, h2 for section headings |
| Reading / Focus order | Thread header → Comment list (top to bottom) → Comment input |
| Accessible names | Comment items have aria-label with author + preview |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through comments, Enter/Space expands long body |
| Target size | Comment items ≥24×24 CSS px, submit button ≥44×44 CSS px |
| Focus not obscured | Thread header sticky, comments scroll beneath |
| Non-color intent | Author name + avatar, not color alone |

---

## Assumptions & Open Questions

1. **Toast container position**: Assumed bottom-right for desktop, top for mobile. Confirm with design team.
2. **Modal dismiss behavior**: Critical errors (auth_failed, forbidden) require button click, not overlay click. Confirm with UX requirements.
3. **Animation timing**: Pulsing animation assumed 1s infinite for connecting/reconnecting states. Confirm with motion design guidelines.
4. **Toast auto-dismiss timing**: Rate limited toast shows countdown, invalid channel auto-dismisses after 5s. Confirm with UX requirements.
5. **Issue Board real-time update behavior**: Assumed card animates to new column on status change, brief highlight on other updates. Confirm with motion design guidelines.
6. **Notification Panel overlay behavior**: Assumed panel overlays content (not pushes). Confirm with layout requirements.
7. **Comment Thread new comment placement**: Assumed new comments append at bottom (not inline for replies). Confirm with threading model.
8. **Missing DS Card component**: §5 Issue Board and §7 Comment Thread use "Generic card" as a placeholder. The design-system does not define a Card component. The DS owner should define one before the hi-fi pass. Until then, the card layout is: title, assignee, priority, labels (for issues); author, avatar, timestamp, body (for comments).
9. **Optional DS layout primitives**: §5 Board Column uses "Generic container", §5/§7 Board/Thread Header uses "Generic header", and §6 Notification Panel uses "Generic list item". These are structural layout elements not defined in the design-system. The DS owner may optionally define `Container`, `Header`, and `ListItem` components for consistency across screens. Not blocking for buildability.

